# Bot-wall block rate on large EU shops

Measured 2026-11-03 around 20:45 CET by builder-core, from one residential connection in Czechia, with the CLI (`pnpm cli scan <host> --json`): one request per site, the scanner's own user agent (`Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; eaa-check/0.1; accessibility checker by studio9)`), no retries, no evasion.

## Result

9 of 16 home pages blocked the scanner. 6 were read and checked. 1 sent a JavaScript shell with nothing to check.

| Site | HTTP | Outcome | Wall |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| zalando.de | 200 | checked, empty shell | none seen; content built by JavaScript |
| otto.de | 200 | checked | none |
| bol.com | 403 | refused | refusal status, vendor not named |
| cdiscount.com | 200 | refused | Baleen JavaScript challenge |
| fnac.com | 200 | checked | none |
| elcorteingles.es | 200 | checked | none |
| mediamarkt.de | 403 | refused | Cloudflare |
| ikea.com | 200 | checked | none |
| decathlon.fr | 403 | refused | Cloudflare |
| allegro.pl | 403 | refused | DataDome |
| emag.ro | 200 | checked | none |
| alza.cz | 403 | refused | Cloudflare |
| notino.cz | 403 | refused | Cloudflare |
| mall.cz | 403 | refused | DataDome |
| rohlik.cz | 200 | checked | none |
| booking.com | 202 | refused | AWS WAF JavaScript challenge |

## Gotcha found on the way

booking.com (HTTP 202) and cdiscount.com (HTTP 200) answered with challenge pages the detector did not know, so the first run reported findings about a challenge page (`document-title` on booking, `html-lang` on cdiscount). One diagnostic request each showed the markers: AWS WAF's `AwsWafIntegration` plus `/challenge.js`, and Baleen's `__blnChallengeStore`. Both are now in `CHALLENGE_BODIES` (`packages/core/src/challenge.ts`, test in `packages/core/test/challenge.test.ts`), and both sites now get the blocked report. A wall the detector does not know still yields findings about the wall; the outcome text and the "empty shell" note are the only guard.

## What it means for the axe round

- More than half of large shops refuse a plain fetch from a scanner that names itself. Static checks alone will tell most big e-commerce visitors "this site blocked automated checks".
- Whether Browser Run gets further is untested here: it needs the deployed Worker. Cloudflare-fronted shops may treat Cloudflare's own browser differently from a residential fetch; DataDome, AWS WAF and Baleen run JavaScript challenges that a real browser may pass on its own. Repeat this list through Browser Run after the deploy, same one-request rule, and record it below this table.
- Never evade: no user-agent spoofing, no challenge solving, no retries to wear a wall down.

## Through the deployed product, with Browser Run

Measured 2026-11-03 around 21:10 CET by builder-cloud, on stage `dev` (scanner commit `f3eaa24` plus two adapter fixes, see below): one `startScan` per site through the page's RPC, then polling `getScan`. Same rules: the scanner's own user agent, one scan each, no retries, no evasion. The static fetch now leaves from Cloudflare's network, not a residential line. The rendered step runs only when the static report is `checked`, so Browser Run was tried on the 6 sites the static fetch read.

### Result

6 of 16 shops got a rendered audit. Browser Run was not blocked on any of the 6 it opened. The other 10 refused the static fetch from Cloudflare, so the browser was never tried on them.

| Site | Static from Cloudflare | Residential (above) | Browser Run | axe rules failing |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| zalando.de | refused, HTTP 403 | checked | not tried | |
| otto.de | checked | checked | ran | color-contrast, image-alt, label-content-name-mismatch, link-name |
| bol.com | refused, HTTP 403 | refused | not tried | |
| cdiscount.com | refused, Baleen | refused | not tried | |
| fnac.com | refused, DataDome 403 | checked | not tried | |
| elcorteingles.es | refused, HTTP 403 | checked | not tried | |
| mediamarkt.de | checked | refused, Cloudflare | ran | aria-required-children, aria-required-parent, label-content-name-mismatch, link-name, listitem |
| ikea.com | checked | checked | ran | label-content-name-mismatch, list |
| decathlon.fr | refused, Cloudflare 403 | refused | not tried | |
| allegro.pl | refused, DataDome 403 | refused | not tried | |
| emag.ro | checked, HTTP 511 | checked | ran | color-contrast, label-content-name-mismatch |
| alza.cz | checked | refused, Cloudflare | ran | color-contrast |
| notino.cz | refused, Cloudflare 403 | refused | not tried | |
| mall.cz | refused, DataDome 403 | refused | not tried | |
| rohlik.cz | checked | checked | ran | color-contrast, label-content-name-mismatch, list |
| booking.com | refused, AWS WAF 202 | refused | not tried | |

Each rendered audit took 9 to 17 seconds end to end, including the static step. Six reservations of 60 seconds used 360 of the 1080 daily browser seconds.

### What it means

- Leaving from Cloudflare changes who blocks, not how many: 10 of 16 refused, against 9 of 16 residential. Two Cloudflare-fronted shops (mediamarkt.de, alza.cz) let the Worker through and refused the residential line; three shops that let the residential line through (zalando.de, fnac.com, elcorteingles.es) refuse Cloudflare's addresses.
- zalando.de sent an empty JavaScript shell residentially. Behind a real browser it would be the most useful case for the rendered check, and from Cloudflare it is refused before the browser is tried.
- Whether Browser Run passes the walls that refuse the static fetch is still unmeasured. Proposal for the lead and Vojta: run the rendered step on a `refused` static report too, within the same budget, and show its findings when the browser got the page. It costs browser seconds on sites likely to block, and it changes what a refused report shows, so it is a product call. One more measurement on these 10 sites would answer it.

### Fixed on the way

- `step` in `packages/browser-audit/src/browser-session.ts` handed its function to `Effect.tryPromise`, which calls it with an AbortSignal. The bound `page.setUserAgent(userAgent)` then received the signal as its `userAgentMetadata`, and Chrome refused the call ("Failed to deserialize params.userAgentMetadata.architecture"). Every rendered audit failed with "The browser service failed". Now the function is called with no argument; test in `packages/browser-audit/test/browser-session.test.ts`.
- `axe.source` is `axeFunction.toString()`. Alchemy's Rolldown build wraps axe-core's CommonJS, renames `module` to `u` and minifies `typeof module === "undefined"` to `u === void 0`, so the injected script threw "u is not defined". The adapter now injects axe-core's shipped `axe.min.js` as text (`?raw` import, Vite in tests, `apps/scanner/src/raw-text-plugin.ts` in the Worker build), which no bundler transforms.

## Browser Run on statically refused shops

Measured 2026-11-03 around 21:15 CET by builder-cloud on stage `dev`, after the lead approved running the rendered check on refused static reports (Browser Run is an honest Cloudflare browser with the scanner's own user agent, so it is no evasion). One new scan per shop on the `www.` address, because the bare address was reused within the hour. The outcome per shop comes from the Workflow's log line `Rendered check of <url> after a <outcome> fetch: <result>`.

The daily browser budget (1080 seconds, 60 reserved per scan) ran out during this round, after 18 reservations that day, so only 5 of the 10 refused shops reached the browser.

| Site | Static from Cloudflare | Browser Run |
| --- | --- | --- |
| zalando.de | refused, HTTP 403 | ran |
| cdiscount.com | refused, Baleen | ran |
| elcorteingles.es | refused, HTTP 403 | ran |
| bol.com | refused, HTTP 403 | blocked |
| fnac.com | refused, DataDome 403 | blocked |
| decathlon.fr | refused | ran |
| allegro.pl | refused | blocked |
| notino.cz | refused | ran |
| mall.cz | refused | blocked |
| booking.com | refused | ran |

The last 5 rows were measured the same evening after decision 22 (dev budget 5400 seconds a day, measured session time). Result: 6 of 10 statically refused shops let Browser Run in (zalando, cdiscount, elcorteingles, decathlon, notino, booking) and 4 block it too (bol, fnac, allegro, mall). With the 6 shops the static fetch read, 12 of 16 shops get a rendered audit. A rescan of www.notino.cz after the per-probe timeouts (commit 07bde2a) gave rendered findings for reflow, text spacing and target size; its tab walk was not judged.

Gotcha (fixed by decision 22, the unused part is now released): a scan reserved 60 seconds but a rendered audit took 9 to 25 seconds, so the budget fills about four times faster than the browser is used. Releasing the unused part of a reservation after the audit would give roughly 60 to 100 rendered audits a day in place of 18.
